# Trivy ignore file for the BWS security scan ( BWS-only, under .github ).
# Passed to trivy-action via the `trivyignores` input.
#
# Every entry below is a known-vulnerable JavaScript package that reaches Koha
# only as a TRANSITIVE BUILD/DEV-TIME dependency: the OpenAPI docs bundler
# ( @redocly/cli -> redoc -> dompurify ), the asset build chain ( webpack /
# rspack / gulp / cypress -> handlebars, protobufjs, immutable, picomatch,
# brace-expansion, tmp, fast-uri, postcss, etc. ). None of them are shipped to
# browsers ( verified absent from the built Vue bundles under
# koha-tmpl/*/js/vue/dist ), so they are not reachable in a deployed Koha.
#
# This is a point-in-time list. New advisories in these packages will surface
# as fresh alerts ( on purpose ) for re-triage; do not blanket-ignore by
# package. If any of these ever becomes a runtime/shipped dependency, drop it
# from this file and treat it as a real finding.

